{"id": "1548887359255351296", "channel_id": "1548887359255351296", "author_id": "375785840858628109", "author_name": "trunglebob", "content": "Used to play quite frequently months ago but sometime around June/July, it started crashing every time I got past \"Logging in to User Center\" or whatever it says. I have an IT background so I've been on and off trying whatever I can think of to fix this problem and play the game <a:manscrying:796293907788988446> Here's a link to the log (essentially identical every time it crashes): https://pastebin.com/VmpqqMJ5\n\nWhat I've tried so far:\nSteam file integrity verification and full clean reinstall\nAll overlays disabled (Steam, Discord, NVIDIA, Windows Game Bar)\nUnity Graphics Jobs disabled via boot.config (gfx-enable-gfx-jobs=0)\nNVIDIA power management set to \"Prefer maximum performance\"\nDLDSR fully disabled\nForced dGPU via Windows Graphics settings (system has a secondary AMD iGPU)\nTwo different NVIDIA driver versions\nGPU/driver stability confirmed clean via FurMark stress test (10+ min, stable clocks/temps, zero errors)\nNo corresponding TDR/driver-reset event in Windows Event Viewer System log at time of crash — the device removal appears client-side, not an actual driver crash\nDeleted all local PlayerPrefs/cache data (AppData/LocalLow/Morimens, com.Morimens.pc, com_Morimens_pc)", "timestamp": "2026-09-14T02:45:23.382000+00:00", "thread_id": "1548887359255351296", "embeds": [{"type": "link", "title": "Input System module state changed to: Initialized.Loading player da...", "url": "https://pastebin.com/VmpqqMJ5", "description": "Pastebin.com is the number one paste tool since 2002. Pastebin is a website where you can store text online for a set period of time."}], "thread_title": "Can't play the game (Crashing)", "forum_channel_id": "1180845276823564288", "thread_tags": ["1542484376573583380", "1542484945447026708"], "is_thread_starter": true}
